      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;achilles-tendonitis-embolizationtame&#34;&gt;Achilles Tendonitis Embolization(TAME)&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A minimally invasive treatment for chronic Achilles tendon pain&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h1 id=&#34;understanding-achilles-tendonitis&#34;&gt;Understanding Achilles Tendonitis&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Pain at the back of your heel can make walking or even standing difficult. Achilles tendonitis (also called Achilles tendinopathy) is a common cause of this discomfort—especially in people who are active or on their feet for long hours.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h1 id=&#34;what-is-the-achilles-tendon&#34;&gt;What is the Achilles Tendon?&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The Achilles tendon is the strongest tendon in your body.&#xA;It connects your calf muscles to your heel bone and plays a key role in movements such as:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
